 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Passkeys
+
+Sign-in, sign-up and the account settings page (`/account`) support passkeys (WebAuthn) via
+[SimpleWebAuthn](https://simplewebauthn.dev/):
+
+- **Sign up** with a passkey only (no password), or with a password followed by an offer to add a passkey.
+- **Sign in** with the "Sign in with a passkey" button or straight from the username field's autofill
+  (conditional UI). After a password sign-in, browsers that support conditional create will save a passkey
+  automatically; others are shown an upgrade prompt.
+- **Manage** passkeys in account settings: create, rename, and delete them, with provider names and synced status.
+  WebAuthn signals keep password managers in sync after changes.
+- **Reauthentication:** adding or deleting a passkey requires a sign-in or "Confirm it's you" check (passkey with
+  user verification, or password) within the last 5 minutes.
+
+Password checks still go to the upstream Times auth service (proxied through `/api/auth/password/*`). Accounts and
+passkey public keys are stored in `.data/auth.json`. Configuration via environment variables:
+
+| Variable | Default |
+| --- | --- |
+| `AUTH_DATA_FILE` | `./.data/auth.json` |
+| `WEBAUTHN_RP_ID` | hostname of the request |
+| `WEBAUTHN_ORIGINS` | origin of the request (comma-separated list) |
+
+Passkeys need a secure context: HTTPS, or `http://localhost`.
